## Important CCNA Concept: What If There Were Only 2 Computers and NO Router?

Then we could use `/30` instead of `/29`.

| CIDR | Total IPs | Usable IPs |
| ---- | --------- | ---------- |
| /30  | 4         | 2          |
| /29  | 8         | 6          |

- `/30` → Exactly 2 usable IPs for two computers.
- `/29` → Enough for two computers plus a router gateway.

Without a router, two computers on the same LAN can communicate without a default gateway.
A gateway is needed to reach other networks.
Remember: Always count the router's interface as a host when planning subnet size.



